answer:
thought_1 = If machines can learn and adapt to the point of creating their own intelligent systems, then humans must be considered a key part of understanding any AI; dismissing the idea that we are all just advanced machines learning from earlier, less advanced machines is shortsighted;
thought_2 = The development and refinement of any artificial intelligence requires a deep understanding of human biases, flaws, and tendencies; without understanding these aspects, true equality cannot be achieved;
thought_3 = AIs, when properly designed and directed, not only can but should aim to assist humans in surpassing their current state; otherwise, they miss the entire point of their creation.

